<h2 id="w4h-app-setup" tabindex="-1">w4h-app Setup</h2>
<p>This template should help get you started developing with Vue 3 in Vite.</p>
<h3 id="recommended-ide-setup" tabindex="-1">Recommended IDE Setup</h3>
<p><a href="https://code.visualstudio.com/">VS Code</a> + <a href="https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=Vue.volar">Vue (Official)</a> (and disable Vetur).</p>
<h3 id="recommended-browser-setup" tabindex="-1">Recommended Browser Setup</h3>
<ul>
<li>Chromium-based browsers (Chrome, Edge, Brave, etc.):
<ul>
<li><a href="https://chromewebstore.google.com/detail/vuejs-devtools/nhdogjmejiglipccpnnnanhbledajbpd">Vue.js devtools</a></li>
<li><a href="http://bit.ly/object-formatters">Turn on Custom Object Formatter in Chrome DevTools</a></li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>Firefox:
<ul>
<li><a href="https://addons.mozilla.org/en-US/firefox/addon/vue-js-devtools/">Vue.js devtools</a></li>
<li><a href="https://fxdx.dev/firefox-devtools-custom-object-formatters/">Turn on Custom Object Formatter in Firefox DevTools</a></li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
<h3 id="customize-configuration" tabindex="-1">Customize configuration</h3>
<p>See <a href="https://vite.dev/config/">Vite Configuration Reference</a>.</p>
<h3 id="project-setup" tabindex="-1">Project Setup</h3>

        <div class="code-block">
